On 21 Sep., 06:49, Ben Rosengart <ben+r...@panix.com> wrote:
> If I throw a missile weapon, I probably want to pick it up when I
> see it again. =A0Yay for autopickup. =A0But if I throw anything else,
> I'm probably just getting it out of the way. =A0Suggestion: create
> an option to autopickup missile weapons only.

That's already possible on NAO with autopickup exceptions, or you
could use the pickup_thrown patch at home.

The relevant sections of my config are below. It assumes you either
don't individually name objects, or you name it something the rest of
the autopickup config checks. Pickup_types must not be empty,
therefore the iron balls.

OPTIONS=3Dautopickup
OPTIONS=3Dpickup_types:0
OPTIONS=3Dpickup_burden:unencumbered

# # ammo for me
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*dagger named !C*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*dagger named C*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<* named ammo*"

# #ammo monsters shouldn't get
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*arrow"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*elven arrow"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*orcish arrow"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*silver arrow"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*ya"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*crossbow bolt"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*dart"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*shuriken"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*dagger"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*elven dagger"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*orcish dagger"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*silver dagger"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*athame"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*knife"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*runed arrow"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*crude arrow"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*bamboo arrow"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*throwing star"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*runed dagger"
## AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D"<*crude dagger"

# #Misc junk. Never pick up iron balls so pickup_types can be "0" if
you only want exceptions.
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=3D">*heavy iron ball*"


